  "id": "deadspaceinteriors",
  "neon": "#4affd0",
  "note": "DEAD SPACE INTERIORS, the furniture showroom. The tile's prose: a decommissioned industrial unit with the roller door cut out and replaced by plate glass, so what the road sees is a lit showroom floor inside a shell that still has the old crane rail bolted across its ceiling. Two armchairs and a standard lamp are staged on a rug out on the forecourt, in the weather.\n\nSo it is the unit: a corrugated shed under a three-tooth north-light roof, portal-frame columns down both flanks, the works office in brick at one front corner, and the roller door still on the back. The front opening is glazed and lit warm, the name is painted on the sheeting the way a works names itself, and the crane rail's runway beam still pokes out over the glass with its hoist block on it. The armchairs, the rug and the lamp are on the forecourt.\n\nIt replaced a teal cross-plan lantern in marble, the same template as the Cherry Pit and Second Skin beside it.\n\n⚠ THE FORECOURT FURNITURE IS MASS, not detail: there is no detail kind for a chair. Each piece is a box a few hundredths across standing on the ground in front of the glass, so it never crosses the glazing or the sign.",
  "pal": "ty_wh_metal",
  "replaces": "showroom",
